Like That?."},{"season":"2024","heading":"2024: BAHAHAHA","text":"Under Elis, BAHAHAHA went 6-8 to finish as the No. 6 seed, scoring 1784.98 points, 6th in the league. [[p:3163|Jared Goff]] led the club with 299.72 points in 15 starts, followed by [[p:4018|Joe Mixon]] (236.70). The season high was 159.24 in week 6 ([[g:2024-06-6-10]]). In the Dynasty Playoffs they beat [[f:6|got that DAWG]] 126.80-120.80 in the First Round, then lost to [[f:5|i’m Stroud of you]] 107.50-164.30 in the Semifinal, then lost to [[f:8|Breece is the Word]] 105.30-170.30 in the Third Place Game and finished 4th. The front office made 35 transactions, 2 of them trades. The club was renamed 4 times during the year, ending as BAHAHAHA. [[m:ritesh]] gave up his stake on 2024-05-12."},{"season":"2025","heading":"2025: Maddison Beer’s Boys","text":"Under Elis, Maddison Beer’s Boys went 6-8 to finish as the No. 8 seed, scoring 1705.89 points, 8th in the league. [[p:11560|Caleb Williams]] led the club with 280.10 points in 15 starts, followed by [[p:3163|Jared Goff]] (279.74). The season high was 171.06 in week 9 ([[g:2025-09-7-10]]). In the Toilet Bowl they beat [[f:11|BubbaNASTIES]] 162.70-143.42 in the Toilet Bowl First Round, then beat [[f:3|Kolkata Kommies]] 168.11-98.66 in the Seventh Place Game and finished 7th. The front office made 23 transactions, 0 of them trades. Young Sexy Award winners on the roster at season's end: Harold Fannin (TE). The club was renamed 1 time during the year, ending as Maddison Beer’s Boys."},{"season":"2026","heading":"2026: Maddison Beer’s Boys","text":"Through 4 games under Elis, Maddison Beer’s Boys are 2-2 and 8th in the standings, with 452.00 points (10th). [[p:3257|Jacoby Brissett]] led the club with 60.52 points in 4 starts, followed by [[p:12490|Bhayshul Tuten]] (58.10). The season high was 122.92 in week 2 ([[g:2026-02-4-10]]). The front office made 29 transactions, 5 of them trades."}]}